doc:Factsarticle1_101 schema:abstract "Misalignment faults in drive systems occur when the motor and load are not properly aligned, leading to deviations in the centerlines of the coupled shafts. The study investigates misalignment faults in synchronous reluctance motors by analyzing vibration and current signals under different load conditions and operating speeds."@en .
